---

---

<section class="relative z-10 mx-auto w-full max-w-3xl border-t border-gray-200/50 px-6 py-32">
  <div class="mb-20 text-left">
    <h2 class="text-heading-32 sm:text-heading-40 text-gray-1000 font-bold tracking-tight">FAQ</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="space-y-2">
    <!-- FAQ 1 -->
    <details class="group border-b border-gray-200 py-6 [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
      <summary
        class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-1.5 rounded-sm focus-visible:outline-none"
      >
        <h3 class="text-gray-1000 text-sm font-semibold sm:text-base">
          Is my identity really anonymous?
        </h3>
        <span class="relative h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-gray-500">
          <svg
            class="absolute inset-0 h-4 w-4 opacity-100 transition-opacity group-open:opacity-0"
            fill="none"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
          >
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 4v16m8-8H4"></path>
          </svg>
          <svg
            class="absolute inset-0 h-4 w-4 opacity-0 transition-opacity group-open:opacity-100"
            fill="none"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
          >
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M20 12H4"></path>
          </svg>
        </span>
      </summary>
      <p class="mt-4 text-xs leading-relaxed text-gray-600 sm:text-sm">
        Yes. Your university email is processed strictly to confirm active student status. The
        system generates a hash to prevent abuse and deletes the raw email address immediately. No
        student IDs or names are saved.
      </p>
    </details>

    <!-- FAQ 2 -->
    <details class="group border-b border-gray-200 py-6 [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
      <summary
        class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-1.5 rounded-sm focus-visible:outline-none"
      >
        <h3 class="text-gray-1000 text-sm font-semibold sm:text-base">Who are the Peer Mentors?</h3>
        <span class="relative h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-gray-500">
          <svg
            class="absolute inset-0 h-4 w-4 opacity-100 transition-opacity group-open:opacity-0"
            fill="none"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
          >
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 4v16m8-8H4"></path>
          </svg>
          <svg
            class="absolute inset-0 h-4 w-4 opacity-0 transition-opacity group-open:opacity-100"
            fill="none"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
          >
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M20 12H4"></path>
          </svg>
        </span>
      </summary>
      <p class="mt-4 text-xs leading-relaxed text-gray-600 sm:text-sm">
        Peer mentors are upper-year students who have been verified by the university
        administration. They undergo specialized training in active support, boundaries, and crisis
        escalation protocols.
      </p>
    </details>

    <!-- FAQ 3 -->
    <details class="group border-b border-gray-200 py-6 [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
      <summary
        class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-1.5 rounded-sm focus-visible:outline-none"
      >
        <h3 class="text-gray-1000 text-sm font-semibold sm:text-base">
          What happens in a crisis situation?
        </h3>
        <span class="relative h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-gray-500">
          <svg
            class="absolute inset-0 h-4 w-4 opacity-100 transition-opacity group-open:opacity-0"
            fill="none"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
          >
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 4v16m8-8H4"></path>
          </svg>
          <svg
            class="absolute inset-0 h-4 w-4 opacity-0 transition-opacity group-open:opacity-100"
            fill="none"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
          >
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M20 12H4"></path>
          </svg>
        </span>
      </summary>
      <p class="mt-4 text-xs leading-relaxed text-gray-600 sm:text-sm">
        This platform is for peer support and is not a clinical treatment tool. If a student is in
        crisis, mentors follow strict escalation protocols to provide direct links and hotlines to
        professional emergency healthcare resources.
      </p>
    </details>

    <!-- FAQ 4 -->
    <details class="group border-b border-gray-200 py-6 [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
      <summary
        class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-1.5 rounded-sm focus-visible:outline-none"
      >
        <h3 class="text-gray-1000 text-sm font-semibold sm:text-base">
          How do administrators manage the platform?
        </h3>
        <span class="relative h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-gray-500">
          <svg
            class="absolute inset-0 h-4 w-4 opacity-100 transition-opacity group-open:opacity-0"
            fill="none"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
          >
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 4v16m8-8H4"></path>
          </svg>
          <svg
            class="absolute inset-0 h-4 w-4 opacity-0 transition-opacity group-open:opacity-100"
            fill="none"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
          >
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M20 12H4"></path>
          </svg>
        </span>
      </summary>
      <p class="mt-4 text-xs leading-relaxed text-gray-600 sm:text-sm">
        Admin dashboard accounts are reserved for verified university administrators. Staff can view
        aggregated, non-identifying platform usage metrics, approve peer mentors, manage
        announcements, and audit reported content.
      </p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
